# ---------------- Amelia Earhart ----------------
meta={
"type":"tale","title_zh":"埃尔哈特：最后一段没有降落的航线","title_en":"Amelia Earhart: The Last Leg That Never Landed",
"era":"1937 年 7 月 2 日","era_en":"2 July 1937",
"region":"太平洋，莱城至豪兰岛航线","region_en":"Pacific Ocean, Lae to Howland Island",
"coords":[0.8,176.6],"tags":["埃尔哈特","航空","太平洋","失踪","1937"],"collections":[],"credibility":"verified",
"related":["mh370","carroll-a-deering"],
"en_headings":["A flying career","The round-the-world route","Vanishing near Howland","The main hypotheses","What the archives show","Legacy and the search continues"],
"limits_zh":"埃尔哈特与努南的最终位置没有确认。坠海、在尼库马罗罗礁搁浅、被日方俘获等假说都缺少决定性物证；无线电信号、照片、骨骼和声呐图像各自能支持一部分，却不能拼成完整链条。1937 年的搜索记录、美国海军与海岸警卫队日志、普渡大学档案和民间调查，质量与用途并不相同。本文把“已确认的航线和失踪时间”与“后来的推测”分开，不把纪录片或单张照片当作结案证据。",
"limits_en":"The final location of Earhart and Noonan has not been confirmed. The crash-and-sink, Nikumaroro strandings, and Japanese capture hypotheses all lack decisive physical evidence; radio signals, photographs, bones, and sonar images each support a part but do not complete a chain. The 1937 search records, US Navy and Coast Guard logs, Purdue archives, and private investigations differ in quality and purpose. This entry separates the confirmed route and loss time from later speculation and does not treat a documentary or a single photograph as closing evidence.",
}
sections=[
("一、飞行生涯","阿梅莉亚·埃尔哈特 1897 年生于美国堪萨斯州阿奇森，1920 年代成为飞行员。1928 年，她作为乘客参加跨大西洋飞行，成为第一位飞越大西洋的女性；1932 年，她独自驾机从纽芬兰飞往北爱尔兰，完成单人跨大西洋飞行。1935 年，她从夏威夷飞往加州，证明太平洋航线可行。她的名声不只来自飞行，也来自写作、演讲和推动女性航空教育。","Amelia Earhart was born in Atchison, Kansas, in 1897 and became a pilot in the 1920s. In 1928 she crossed the Atlantic as a passenger, becoming the first woman to fly across the ocean; in 1932 she flew solo from Newfoundland to Northern Ireland, completing a solo transatlantic flight. In 1935 she flew from Hawaii to California, proving a Pacific route. Her fame came not only from flying but from writing, lecturing, and promoting aviation education for women."),
("二、环球航线","1937 年，埃尔哈特尝试沿赤道方向环球飞行。她与 navigator 弗雷德·努南驾驶一架双引擎洛克希德 Electra，从奥克兰出发，经夏威夷、豪兰岛、莱城、达尔文、印度、非洲，再回到美国。6 月 29 日，他们从莱城起飞，目标是 2,200 英里外的豪兰岛；7 月 2 日，飞机在接近豪兰岛时失去联系。豪兰岛只是一个狭长的珊瑚礁，跑道和导航设施都很有限。","In 1937 Earhart attempted a round-the-world flight along an equatorial route. With navigator Fred Noonan she flew a twin-engine Lockheed Electra from Oakland via Hawaii, Howland Island, Lae, Darwin, India, and Africa, then back toward the United States. On 29 June they took off from Lae for Howland Island, 2,200 miles away; on 2 July the aircraft lost contact near Howland. Howland is only a narrow coral island with a short runway and limited navigation aids."),
("三、消失与搜索","美国海军与海岸警卫队展开了当时规模最大的海上搜索之一，持续两周多，出动多艘军舰和飞机，覆盖太平洋大片海域，没有找到飞机残骸或 survivors。海岸警卫队的“伊塔斯卡”号在豪兰岛附近接收过无线电信号，但信号方向模糊，无法定位。最后的无线电内容、油量消耗和天气条件，成为后来所有假说的起点。","The US Navy and Coast Guard mounted one of the largest sea searches of the time, lasting more than two weeks with multiple ships and aircraft over a vast area of the Pacific, without finding wreckage or survivors. The Coast Guard cutter Itasca, near Howland, received radio signals, but the bearings were ambiguous and could not fix a position. The final radio messages, fuel consumption, and weather are the starting point for every later hypothesis."),
("四、主要假说","最直接的解释是飞机在燃油耗尽后坠入太平洋，残骸沉没或未被发现。另一种假说认为，飞机在尼库马罗罗礁（现属基里巴斯）搁浅，机组在岛上生存了一段时间；支持者引用 1940 年发现的骨骼、鞋具和无线电信号，但骨骼后来遗失，鉴定也有争议。第三种假说认为两人被日军俘获并关押，证据多为口述与推测。每种假说都能解释部分事实，却都无法排除其他可能。","The most direct explanation is that the aircraft ran out of fuel and crashed into the Pacific, with wreckage sinking or never found. Another hypothesis holds that the plane landed on Nikumaroro reef, now in Kiribati, and the crew survived for a time; supporters cite bones, shoes, and radio signals found in 1940, but the bones were later lost and their identification is disputed. A third hypothesis says the two were captured and held by Japanese forces, resting mainly on oral accounts and inference. Each explains some facts but cannot exclude the others."),
("五、档案能证明什么","普渡大学的埃尔哈特档案保存了飞行计划、通信、照片和剪报；美国国家档案与海军日志记录了搜索航迹；国际无线电监听记录提供了信号时间。它们能确认出发时间、航线、最后联络和搜索范围，却不能确认飞机最终位置。2010 年代以后，私人调查使用声呐、卫星图像和水下摄影，2024 年曾公布一张声呐图像，但专家普遍认为不足以证明是 Electra。档案的空白，正是各种传说的生长空间。","Purdue University's Earhart archive holds flight plans, correspondence, photographs, and clippings; US national archives and Navy logs record the search tracks; international radio monitoring records give signal times. They can confirm departure, route, last contact, and search area, but not the aircraft's final location. Since the 2010s private searches have used sonar, satellite imagery, and underwater photography; a sonar image was published in 2024, but experts generally consider it insufficient to prove it was the Electra. The gap in the archive is exactly where legends grow."),
("六、遗产与仍在继续的搜索","埃尔哈特成为女性航空、冒险和名人文化的象征。她的失踪被写进书籍、电影、歌曲和阴谋论，尼库马罗罗礁、豪兰岛和日本拘留营都成了叙事地点。对研究者而言，最重要的是把“象征”与“证据”分开：她的飞行纪录可以核实，最后时刻不能。搜索仍在继续，但每一次新图像或新文件出现，都需要同样的检验：来源、链条、可重复性。","Earhart became a symbol of women's aviation, adventure, and celebrity culture. Her disappearance entered books, films, songs, and conspiracy theories, with Nikumaroro, Howland, and Japanese camps becoming narrative locations. For researchers, the priority is to separate symbol from evidence: her flight records can be verified, her final hours cannot. Searches continue, but every new image or document needs the same tests: provenance, chain of custody, and reproducibility."),
]
